      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Selection news",
          "heading": "Semisi Tupou Ta'eiloa signs two-year deal with Super Rugby champions Hurricanes",
          "body": "Former Moana Pasifika back-rower Semisi Tupou Ta'eiloa has committed his future to the Hurricanes, signing a two-year contract with the reigning Super Rugby Pacific champions. The 22-year-old earned his maiden All Blacks call-up during this year's Rugby's Greatest Rivalry series, featuring in mid-week matches against the Sharks and the Lions. Hurricanes head coach Clark Laidlaw praised the forward’s “destructive power,” stating: “He’s someone who has already played Super Rugby at such a high level and played so well at such a young age.”"
